      "headers": [
        "Position",
        "Core Claim",
        "Strength",
        "Weakness"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "**Scientific realism**",
          "True approximately; unobservables exist",
          "No-miracles; IBE natural",
          "Pessimistic meta-induction"
        ],
        [
          "**Constructive empiricism**",
          "Aim = empirical adequacy; agnostic on unobservables",
          "Avoids meta-induction; principled",
          "Observable line vague; anti-realism seems arbitrary"
        ],
        [
          "**Epistemic structural realism**",
          "Believe the mathematical structure",
          "Handles meta-induction; explains continuity",
          "What is structure without an object that instantiates it?"
        ],
        [
          "**Ontic structural realism**",
          "Structure is all there is",
          "Connects to category theory, modern physics",
          "Counter-intuitive; objects as primary seems more defensible"
        ],
        [
          "**Entity realism**",
          "Believe in what you can manipulate",
          "Connects belief to practical competence",
          "Theories are needed to manipulate; theory and entity inseparable?"
        ],
        [
          "**Instrumentalism**",
          "Theories are tools; no truth question",
          "Clean; no metaphysics needed",
          "Science aims at truth — dismissing this distorts scientific practice"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "table-3",
      "line": 268,
      "heading_context": "## Decision Cheat Sheet",
      "headers": [
        "Question",
        "Answer"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "What is IBE?",
          "Inference to Best Explanation: believe the hypothesis that best explains the evidence"
        ],
        [
          "What is the no-miracles argument?",
          "Scientific success would be a miracle if theories weren't approximately true about unobservables"
        ],
        [
          "What is the pessimistic meta-induction?",
          "Historical pattern: successful theories are eventually rejected as false; so current ones probably are too"
        ],
        [
          "What is constructive empiricism?",
          "Van Fraassen: theories need only be empirically adequate; belief in unobservables is unnecessary and epistemically unwarranted"
        ],
        [
          "What is structural realism?",
          "Worrall: retain the mathematical structure across theory change; be agnostic about the \"nature\" behind the structure"
        ],
        [
          "What is entity realism?",
          "Hacking: believe in entities you can use as causal tools; don't need the theory to be true"
        ],
        [
          "How does structural realism handle the meta-induction?",
          "Ether eliminated but Fresnel equations retained in Maxwell: the structure was preserved"
        ]
      ]
    }
